{
  "character": "休",
  "summary": {
    "text": "休 means “rest.” Its components form a small scene: a person, written 亻 at the left, leans against a tree, 木. These accounts explain both parts through that scene, making the shape a direct guide to the meaning.",
    "evidence_ids": [
      "E1",
      "E2",
      "E6"
    ]
  },
  "history": [
    {
      "text": "The Shuowen already describes the person as leaning on the tree and defines the character in terms of resting or stopping. This gives the familiar explanation a history beyond its usefulness as a modern memory aid.",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "E3"
      ]
    }
  ],
